<main>
  <%= render "programs/navigation", program: @program, active: "google_calendar" %>
  <h1>Google Calendar</h1>
  <p>Synchronize booked slots for <%= @program.name %> to a private Google calendar. Events include the model's private name, phone, email, gender, and Instagram tagging preferences. The model and organizers receive invitations, updates, and cancellations.</p>
  <p>Only grant calendar access to authorized organizers. Do not use a public calendar. Calendar guests must not forward these private details. Google reminders are disabled.</p>
  <% if @connection&.enabled? %>
    <p>Connected calendar: <%= @connection.calendar_id %></p>
    <p><%= @pending_count %> booking changes awaiting synchronization.</p>
    <%= button_to "Disconnect Google Calendar", program_google_calendar_path(@program), method: :delete %>
    <p>Disconnecting stops synchronization but does not remove existing Google events or invitations. Reconnecting a different calendar leaves events in the old calendar; remove those manually first.</p>
  <% end %>
  <% if GoogleCalendarConnection.configured? %>
    <%= form_with scope: :google_calendar, url: program_google_calendar_path(@program) do |form| %>
      <p><%= form.label :calendar_id, "Google Calendar ID" %><br><%= form.text_field :calendar_id, value: @connection&.calendar_id, required: true, maxlength: 254 %></p>
      <p><label><%= form.check_box :private_calendar, required: true %> This calendar is private and shared only with authorized organizers.</label></p>
      <%= form.submit @connection&.enabled? ? "Reconnect Google Calendar" : "Connect Google Calendar" %>
    <% end %>
  <% else %>
    <p>An administrator must configure the Google OAuth client and start the calendar worker before connecting.</p>
  <% end %>
  <p><%= link_to "Back to Calendar", program_path(@program, section: "calendar") %></p>
</main>
